  "verdict_hot": "Not exceeded: the hottest capsule hour of 30 ERA5 years is 64.3 °C (sunlit, α 0.95, still air, adiabatic base; 2010-08-08T13:00, air 37.4 °C) against the 70 °C EDLC rating — margin 5.7 K; 52.9 °C at α 0.5; shaded (open-sky diffuse only) 49.1 °C. With still-air h_c × 0.7 (the correlation off its home geometry) the sunlit worst is 68.0 °C — margin 2.0 K (the h_c shift alone is 3.6 K), so for a DARK finish in full sun the margin is of the order of the model's own uncertainty, while a light one keeps ≥ 15.0 K. The capsule requirement's upper 85 °C is not approached in this climate. NOT modelled and moving the hot answer UP: sunlit bark conducting through the flange rim; ERA5 smoothing of station maxima.",
